# ── Brier — brier.<domain> → host:3000 (Next.js next start) ──────────────────
#
# COMMITTED COPY of the additive Caddy site block that fronts brier.beyondkaira.com.
# The AUTHORITATIVE copy currently lives in the shared ams-pulse repo at
# deploy/config/Caddyfile.prod (block "brier.{$PULSE_DOMAIN}"); this file exists
# so the routing is self-contained + auditable from THIS repo. Keep the two in
# sync. The shared Caddy (container pulse-prod-caddy-1) also fronts the owner's
# OTHER production apps, so ALWAYS `caddy validate` before reloading — a bad
# config is rejected atomically, never dropped. See deploy/INSTALL.md step 7.
#
# Brier sets its own security headers via next.config.ts (CSP tuned for the
# YouTube receipt embed), so this block only terminates TLS + reverse-proxies —
# no header overrides that would conflict. `header -Server` strips Caddy's
# Server: fingerprint from proxied responses (defense in depth; the global
# HTTP→HTTPS redirect's Server header is a separate shared-Caddy concern).
# Upstream = VPS public IP (same proven host-process path as the AMS block).
brier.{$PULSE_DOMAIN} {
    header -Server
    reverse_proxy 161.97.172.146:3000 {
        header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
        header_up Host {host}
    }
    log {
        output stdout
        format json
        level INFO
    }
}
